(ROOT/'diagrams'/'retrieval_accuracy.csv').write_text('rank,correct,total,accuracy_percent\n2,999,1000,99.9\n4,997,1000,99.7\n6,994,1000,99.4\n',encoding='utf-8')
story += [P('The observed score is the fraction of the 1,000 queries for which the candidate at the specified position has the same class_id. Since each person contributed ten fingers, this also equals the mean of the per-person ten-query scores. It is not rank-k recall: a correct candidate at an earlier rank does not make a later position correct. Mean cosine is a similarity statistic, not a calibrated probability. The complete per-person and query-level results are retained as CSV files in outputs/person_evaluation/densenet121_arcface.'),H('6.3 Interpretation and comparison'),P('On the same retrieval protocol, the earlier ResNet18 ArcFace run yielded exact-position accuracies of 78.9%, 42.5% and 24.7% at positions 2, 4 and 6, respectively. DenseNet results are higher for this sampled benchmark. This observation supports the model choice for this project, but is not a head-to-head claim about operational false-positive rates. The benchmark includes many transformed versions per finger, and the impostor sampling does not represent every possible non-match in a large database.'),H('6.4 Limitations and unmeasured quantities'),P('No validated open-set false-identification rate, independent latent-print evaluation, end-to-end arbitrary-upload study, throughput or latency benchmark, storage-cost analysis, confidence interval, mAP, precision-recall curve or clinical/forensic deployment study is reported. The EER comparison selected a model using the test set, so that same test set is no longer an untouched final holdout for model selection. A new external subject-disjoint dataset is needed for an unbiased final assessment. A separate validation set should establish operational thresholds before the external test.'),H('6.5 Ethical, legal, privacy and security considerations'),P('Fingerprint images and embeddings are sensitive biometric information. A meaningful deployment must establish lawful authority, appropriate consent or other legal basis, retention periods, access restrictions, audit trails, encrypted transmission and storage, key management, incident response and deletion processes appropriate to the applicable jurisdiction. Embeddings can reveal identity-related information and should not be treated as anonymous merely because they are vectors. Source paths and finger identifiers in metadata also require protection.'),P('Ranked candidates should be reviewed using an appropriate forensic workflow. A false match can affect a person even when the score is presented as a candidate; human review should be documented and protected against contextual bias [2]. Model performance should be investigated across image qualities and relevant population groups, using an appropriately governed independent evaluation. No legal compliance certification is claimed by this prototype.')]
story += chapter(7,'Conclusion & Future Scope')
story += [H('7.1 Conclusion'),P('This work demonstrates a research pipeline for learning fixed-length fingerprint features, storing them in a persistent vector database and retrieving candidate matches. DenseNet121 ArcFace achieved the lowest sampled EER among twelve saved checkpoints and was selected for subsequent embedding generation. On the stated closed-set retrieval experiment, the selected exact positions matched finger class in 99.9%, 99.7% and 99.4% of queries. These findings are encouraging for the recorded experimental protocol but are insufficient to establish real-world forensic reliability.'),H('7.2 Future scope'),P('Priority next steps are to evaluate independent fingerprints collected under varied operational conditions; establish a new untouched final holdout after model selection; calibrate thresholds on separate validation data; and measure open-set identification, rank-k recall, mAP, latency and uncertainty. An upload interface should apply the same preprocessing and checkpoint version as enrolment, show traceable candidate metadata and enable an authorised expert to review results.'),P('Further work may investigate calibrated quality gates, minutiae-aware reranking, explainable evidence presentation, domain adaptation and robustness to partial or low-quality prints. Governance work should address privacy, encryption, retention, access control, data provenance and audit logging before any sensitive deployment.')]
